    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> became a republic on 31 May 1961 and left the Commonwealth under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hendrik-verwoerd">Hendrik Verwoerd</a>.</li><li>For three decades it enforced grand apartheid, created ethnic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homelands</a> and fought a border war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">Namibia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angola">Angola</a>.</li><li>Negotiations from 1990 led to the 1994 elections, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a>’s presidency and the democratic constitution of 1996.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> built six nuclear weapons in the 1980s and dismantled them around 1990–1991, the first country to give up a nuclear arsenal it had developed itself.</p></aside>
    </section>

